# Adjudicated `punused` findings for deadset. One reason per group; entries
# match as literal substrings of the finding line, so they never include
# file:line:col -- line numbers shift and an entry with one silently goes stale.
#
# `punused` resolves references through gopls inside this module only and does
# not model interface satisfaction or reflection, so the first two groups are
# its known blind spots rather than dead code. Cross-checked at adjudication
# time: `deadcode -test ./...` reports nothing in this module.

# --- Methods a standard interface calls, never a caller by name.
#
# `MarshalJSON` and `UnmarshalJSON` satisfy `json.Marshaler` and
# `json.Unmarshaler`: encoding/json calls them while it encodes and decodes a
# report, which is what writes a build configuration in its own shape and holds
# every decode of a report to the schemas. `Unwrap` on the refusal type is what
# `errors.Is` and `errors.As` call to reach the refusal's cause, and `Error` is
# what `fmt` calls when a refusal prints through `%v`.
method (Configuration).MarshalJSON is unused
method (*Configuration).UnmarshalJSON is unused
method (ConfigurationNotBuilt).MarshalJSON is unused
method (*ConfigurationNotBuilt).UnmarshalJSON is unused
method (*Report).UnmarshalJSON is unused
method (*Error).Unwrap is unused
method (*Error).Error is used in test only

# --- Members of the report document that only encoding/json reads.
#
# Each field holds one member of the report or finding schema. A decode fills
# it and an encode writes it through reflection, so a report read and written
# again keeps the member, and no Go code names the field while nothing judges
# its value: the finding's test and generated flags, a symbol's container,
# visibility and object path, a component's root flag, and the symbol an edge
# side or a stale suppression names.
field TestOnly is unused
field Generated is unused
field Parent is unused
field Exported is unused
field Objectpath is unused
field Root is unused
field Symbol is unused
field Symbol is used in test only

# --- The report package's surface, which no verb calls yet.
#
# Decode, Encode and the schema version are what the analyze verb's report
# reads, its merge and its verdict call. Each is pinned by the package's own
# suite against the Contract's examples, negatives and merge vectors.
constant SchemaVersion is used in test only
function Decode is used in test only
function Encode is used in test only

# --- Stages the analyze verb calls, which no verb calls yet.
#
# Languages is the language census and Split writes each analyzer's
# configuration section into the run directory; each is pinned by its own
# package's suite.
function Languages is used in test only
method (*Resolved).Split is used in test only
